 L2TP/IPsec does enable the option, but it only works when    per_device_routing is enabled, because adding a blackhole route with    metric (x) to the `main` routing table collides with other metric (x)    routes.  The kernel will not let the two routes coexist, even    temporarily.  So, enable blackhole_ipv6=true on OpenVPN, and always use per-device routing tables if blackhole_ipv6 is enabled.  BUG=chromium:787674 TEST=`ping6 ipv6.google.com` while connected to each VPN TEST=`test_that -b samus network_VPNConnect.openvpn` TEST=`test_that -b samus network_VPNConnect.l2tpipsec_psk`  Change-Id: I7d3359db12d18dd322576ce2c841e297ffe2e13e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/784311 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="784311" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" ref="refs/changes/11/784311/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib050d178dfe1ffef2ba2a32ef11ac3b988e9c14d" commit="5e6edf46b70b1c2fbeefe6b3f55738579bdc59f1" commit_message="Make Linux binary wheels portable  BUG=chromium:787545 TEST=bin/run_tests TEST=rm -rf ~/.cache/cros_venv TEST=in chromeos-admin, bin/test_venv_packages TEST=in autotest, bin/test_lucifer TEST=in chromtie, bin/sysmon --help  Change-Id: Ib050d178dfe1ffef2ba2a32ef11ac3b988e9c14d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/776208 Commit-Ready: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="776208" owner_email="ayatane@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3